menu "BLE Host (shared NimBLE owner)"

    config BLE_HOST_DEVICE_NAME
        string "GAP / advertised device name (max 10 characters)"
        default "NETSHELL32"
        help
            REQ-FUNC-78. Used for the GAP device name and the Complete Local
            Name in the scan response. Kconfig strings carry no length range,
            so ble_host.c enforces 10 characters with a _Static_assert: when
            the OTA service is armed the scan response holds 2 + name + 18
            bytes and must fit 31 bytes.

    config BLE_HOST_MAX_CLIENTS
        int "Maximum number of GATT clients that may register"
        range 2 4
        default 2
        help
            REQ-FUNC-71. Capacity of the compile-time registration table.
            Today: ble_ota and ble_cli.

    config BLE_HOST_EXEC_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Total ble_host_exec() bound used by OTA arm/disarm (ms)"
        range 500 2000
        default 1000
        help
            One deadline covering the exec mutex take, the wait for the
            function to start and the 350 ms completion window
            (tech_spec.md 2.3.5). Sized against the worst-case OTA RX
            callback W_OTA of about 350 ms (tech_spec.md 2.4.9).

    config BLE_HOST_ADV_RETRY_MAX_S
        int "Advertising restart retry ceiling (s)"
        range 5 300
        default 30
        help
            On an advertising start failure the host retries after 1, 2, 4,
            8 and 16 s, then every this many seconds (REQ-REL-03).

    config BLE_HOST_INITIATE_SECURITY
        bool "Request pairing from the peripheral as soon as a peer connects"
        default y
        help
            REQ-FUNC-65. Fallback for the R-02 risk: if the existing OTA
            app misbehaves with peripheral-initiated security, set this to
            n. The CLI still works, because its RX characteristic requires
            an encrypted link and Android pairs on the first write. If
            the fallback is taken, REQ-FUNC-65's "no manual bond step" pass
            criterion is NOT met as written and must be accepted by the
            user (record the deviation in docs/ble_cli.md).

    config BLE_HOST_SECURE_DEADLINE_S
        int "Terminate a link that is not encrypted and bonded after (s)"
        range 10 120
        default 60
        help
            Counted from the connection (and from a secure-to-insecure
            change). A fixed bound, not SMP-progress-aware: a pairing that
            starts after about this long minus a few seconds is cut. The
            default 60 s was confirmed at Gate 2 (G2-09), tech_spec.md 2.3.9.

    config BLE_HOST_SEC_INITIATE_RETRIES
        int "Retries of a failed ble_gap_security_initiate()"
        range 0 3
        default 1
        help
            Each retry is made after 2 s while the link generation is
            unchanged and the link is still not secure. The secure deadline
            applies regardless.

endmenu
